S-COST-2 — Anthropic/LLM cost-path enumeration
Date: 2026-07-30
Method: static grep of api/ for every Anthropic API call site and every
recordAnthropicCost / recordApiCall call site. Read-only; no live query run
(no execute_sql tool available to this agent — same limitation recorded in
DECISIONS.md's D-6 resolution).

Scope note: "spends money" is scoped to Prime's OWN operating cost
(Anthropic/LLM inference), matching the D-6 scope correction already on
record — NOT client ad spend, which PRIME-STRATEGY.md §6 explicitly holds
apart ("Not tracked as Prime cost: Client ad spend. That's the client's
money."). Ad-platform API calls are enumerated separately below for
completeness but are correctly untracked in dollars by design (FLAG 2,
DECISIONS.md D-6 resolution: ad platforms charge per spend, not per call).

=== Anthropic API call sites (the only vendor with a real per-token $ cost) ===

grep 'callClaude(' api/*.js:
  api/chat.js:187        -> detectIntent(), model 'claude-haiku-4-5'
  api/chat.js:760        -> main chat handler, model CHAT_MODEL = 'claude-sonnet-4-6'
  api/analyze-ads.js:200 -> runAnalysisForAccount(), model 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514' (fully dated, no alias)

grep 'recordAnthropicCost(' api/*.js:
  api/chat.js:194        -> event_type 'intent_detection'   [PAIRED with chat.js:187]
  api/chat.js:823        -> event_type 'chat'                [PAIRED with chat.js:760]
  api/analyze-ads.js:236 -> event_type 'analyze_ads'         [PAIRED with analyze-ads.js:200]

RESULT: 3 of 3 Anthropic call sites already call recordAnthropicCost. No
unledgered path found. The defect was not a missing call — it was that
chat.js:760's model (CHAT_MODEL, an alias) could resolve to a dated
snapshot id in the API response that the rate table did not recognize,
producing a silent NULL cost_usd on every priced row despite the ledger
event itself being written (D-6 FLAG 3). Fixed this session:
  - api/lib/cost-rates.js: resolveRateKey() strips a trailing -YYYYMMDD
    suffix before giving up, so any dated resolution of a known alias
    still prices.
  - api/lib/anthropic-cost.js: a model string that still fails to resolve
    now logs "[COST-LEDGER-UNKNOWN-MODEL] eventType=... model=..." before
    the row is written, so a genuinely new/renamed model announces itself
    instead of writing an indistinguishable-from-free NULL.

No other Anthropic/OpenAI/other-LLM vendor call site exists in api/ as of
this commit (grepped for api.openai.com, OPENAI_API_KEY, nanobanana,
dataforseo, perplexity.ai — zero matches). PRIME-STRATEGY.md §6 lists
OpenAI/Perplexity/Nano Banana as APPROVED tools, not yet WIRED — nothing to
enumerate there because nothing calls them yet.

